WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.133 --> 00:00:01.034
Just in to CNN.

00:00:01.034 --> 00:00:01.634
Former President

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.269
Trump has no plans to testify

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:04.337
before a New York grand jury

00:00:04.337 --> 00:00:05.972
investigating those alleged

00:00:05.972 --> 00:00:07.974
hush money payments to Stormy Daniels.

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:09.275
Trump's attorney claims

00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:11.311
if Trump did, in fact, authorize

00:00:11.311 --> 00:00:12.445
the payment to Daniels,

00:00:12.445 --> 00:00:14.781
he did so as a victim of extortion.

00:00:15.215 --> 00:00:16.516
The DEA had invited Trump

00:00:16.516 --> 00:00:18.084
to testify as required

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:19.719
under New York law.

00:00:19.719 --> 00:00:21.187
Trump's former fixer and lawyer,

00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:22.288
Michael Cohen,

00:00:22.288 --> 00:00:23.590
he is expected to provide

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:25.625
additional testimony today.

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:26.793
Well, as Manhattan prosecutors

00:00:26.793 --> 00:00:27.894
weigh whether to charge

00:00:27.894 --> 00:00:28.895
former President Trump,

00:00:28.895 --> 00:00:30.030
he is making his way back

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:30.897
to Iowa tonight,

00:00:30.897 --> 00:00:31.664
his first time in the state

00:00:31.664 --> 00:00:33.233
since launching his third bid

00:00:33.233 --> 00:00:34.567
for the White House.

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:35.969
Despite his legal

00:00:35.969 --> 00:00:37.003
troubles, many Iowa

00:00:37.003 --> 00:00:38.204
voters tell us

00:00:38.204 --> 00:00:40.273
they are still with Trump but

00:00:40.807 --> 00:00:42.075
the same may not be true

00:00:42.075 --> 00:00:44.044
for some of his former campaign officials

00:00:44.044 --> 00:00:45.812
and White House advisers.

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:46.713
CNN's Alina TREENE

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:47.447
joins us now

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:48.214
this morning with her

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:49.949
appointing Elena

00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:51.051
What are you hearing from

00:00:51.051 --> 00:00:52.185
those in Trump's inner circle?

00:00:52.185 --> 00:00:53.186
I mean, we have seen some

00:00:53.186 --> 00:00:53.720
who are in the inner

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:55.989
circle publicly break with him, though,

00:00:55.989 --> 00:00:56.990
limited number.

00:00:56.990 --> 00:00:58.591
You're hearing more in private

00:00:59.859 --> 00:01:01.094
I am, Jim and Erica.

00:01:01.094 --> 00:01:03.496
I reached out to nine former Trump

00:01:03.563 --> 00:01:04.497
campaign officials

00:01:04.497 --> 00:01:06.666
who are with him from 2016

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:08.768
throughout his presidency

00:01:08.768 --> 00:01:09.903
and only three of them

00:01:09.903 --> 00:01:11.004
are publicly willing

00:01:11.004 --> 00:01:11.371
to say

00:01:11.371 --> 00:01:13.406
that they support Donald Trump's

00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:15.141
third White House bid.

00:01:15.141 --> 00:01:16.276
Another three said

00:01:16.276 --> 00:01:18.278
that they wanted to remain neutral

00:01:18.278 --> 00:01:19.279
during the primary

00:01:19.279 --> 00:01:20.013
and the other three

00:01:20.013 --> 00:01:22.048
refused to weigh in for the story

00:01:22.148 --> 00:01:23.016
or do not respond to

00:01:23.016 --> 00:01:24.284
requests for comment.

00:01:24.284 --> 00:01:24.818
And I'll just add,

00:01:24.818 --> 00:01:25.452
I think one of the most

00:01:25.452 --> 00:01:26.453
interesting things

00:01:26.453 --> 00:01:27.220
that I picked up through

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:28.621
the course of my reporting

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:29.389
is about former

00:01:29.389 --> 00:01:31.558
Trump 2016 campaign manager

00:01:31.558 --> 00:01:33.159
Corey Lewandowski.

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:35.395
Lewandowski remained very close

00:01:35.395 --> 00:01:37.530
within Donald Trump's inner circle

00:01:37.597 --> 00:01:39.365
throughout his time in office.

00:01:39.365 --> 00:01:41.234
But I'm told that he's recently

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:42.902
been privately reaching out

00:01:42.902 --> 00:01:44.370
to Republican operatives

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:45.138
and donors,

00:01:45.138 --> 00:01:46.606
telling them not to support

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:49.142
Donald Trump for 20, 24

00:01:49.142 --> 00:01:51.544
and also pitching himself to potential

00:01:51.544 --> 00:01:52.846
other presidential campaigns,

00:01:52.846 --> 00:01:54.180
including that of Governor Ron

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:56.015
DeSantis and Governor Christie.

00:01:56.015 --> 00:01:57.183
Now, Lewandowski

00:01:57.183 --> 00:01:59.552
denied that reporting to CNN,

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:01.454
but I spoke with more than a dozen

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:02.288
of people

00:02:02.288 --> 00:02:03.990
within Trump's orbit who have noted

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:06.192
that Corey has been distancing himself

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:07.193
from Donald Trump

00:02:07.193 --> 00:02:09.562
since the 2020 election.

00:02:09.562 --> 00:02:10.930
We also gave him an opportunity

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:12.232
to reach out

00:02:12.232 --> 00:02:13.366
and endorse

00:02:13.366 --> 00:02:14.701
Donald Trump within the story,

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:16.436
but he refused to do so. Well,

00:02:17.504 --> 00:02:18.404
interesting.

00:02:18.404 --> 00:02:19.372
Elaine, great reporting.

00:02:19.372 --> 00:02:21.141
Appreciate it. Thank you.

00:02:21.141 --> 00:02:23.109
Joining us now to discuss Trump's visit

00:02:23.109 --> 00:02:23.476
to Iowa

00:02:23.476 --> 00:02:24.110
tonight, editor

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:25.311
in chief of the Iowa Capital

00:02:25.311 --> 00:02:26.679
Dispatch, Kathie Obradovich.

00:02:26.679 --> 00:02:27.647
Kathie, good to have you with us.

00:02:27.647 --> 00:02:28.882
This morning.

00:02:28.882 --> 00:02:29.582
If we look at that

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:30.750
reporting from Elaina

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:32.952
in terms of those former

00:02:33.119 --> 00:02:34.320
Trump campaign officials,

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:36.055
the split that we're seeing there.

00:02:36.055 --> 00:02:37.323
What's also interesting

00:02:37.323 --> 00:02:38.892
and you know this better than anyone, is

00:02:38.892 --> 00:02:39.692
when we look at

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:41.461
what the interaction is

00:02:41.461 --> 00:02:43.096
with local officials,

00:02:43.096 --> 00:02:44.664
with elected officials in the state,

00:02:44.664 --> 00:02:45.632
the fact that the governor

00:02:45.632 --> 00:02:46.599
was with

00:02:46.599 --> 00:02:48.168
Governor DeSantis in Iowa

00:02:48.168 --> 00:02:51.171
at two different events, that he was also

00:02:51.171 --> 00:02:54.307
meeting with lawmakers in the state.

00:02:54.607 --> 00:02:55.208
We have reporting

00:02:55.208 --> 00:02:55.842
that Trump is making

00:02:55.842 --> 00:02:57.076
some of those calls privately

00:02:57.076 --> 00:02:57.810
but is there a sense

00:02:57.810 --> 00:02:58.912
this morning of where

00:02:58.912 --> 00:03:01.681
support stands among Iowa lawmakers

00:03:03.716 --> 00:03:04.784
Yeah, I wouldn't read too

00:03:04.784 --> 00:03:05.952
much, Erica, into the fact

00:03:05.952 --> 00:03:07.921
that Governor Reynolds,

00:03:07.921 --> 00:03:08.488
Governor Kim

00:03:08.488 --> 00:03:10.223
Reynolds was appearing with this matter.

00:03:10.223 --> 00:03:10.857
She's appearing

00:03:10.857 --> 00:03:12.458
with every presidential candidate

00:03:12.458 --> 00:03:13.793
that comes to town

00:03:13.793 --> 00:03:15.094
She had events with Nikki

00:03:15.094 --> 00:03:16.296
Haley last month,

00:03:16.296 --> 00:03:17.997
just appeared with Tim Scott.

00:03:17.997 --> 00:03:18.831
She will.

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:19.666
She has appeared

00:03:19.666 --> 00:03:21.000
and I believe she is planning

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.402
to appear with Donald Trump.

00:03:22.402 --> 00:03:24.571
So she's going to be neutral.

00:03:24.604 --> 00:03:27.373
But when we talk to Republicans

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:28.575
at these events

00:03:28.575 --> 00:03:30.476
and it's been a busy four day

00:03:30.476 --> 00:03:32.912
weekend for the Iowa caucus campaign,

00:03:32.912 --> 00:03:36.482
people are not sold on Donald Trump

00:03:36.482 --> 00:03:38.251
for 20, 24.

00:03:38.251 --> 00:03:40.653
They are still he's still very popular

00:03:41.688 --> 00:03:44.090
and he is pulling you know pretty well.

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:45.358
But his polling is down

00:03:45.358 --> 00:03:46.626
from what it was a year ago.

00:03:46.626 --> 00:03:47.727
And Ron DeSantis

00:03:47.727 --> 00:03:48.228
is looking

00:03:48.228 --> 00:03:49.229
like the person

00:03:49.229 --> 00:03:52.532
that Iowa Republicans are kind of eyeing

00:03:52.532 --> 00:03:52.999
to see

00:03:52.999 --> 00:03:54.300
if he can be a substitute

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:56.302
or an alternative candidate.

00:03:56.302 --> 00:03:57.370
Kathy, Iowa voters,

00:03:57.370 --> 00:03:58.438
as you know better than me,

00:03:58.438 --> 00:03:58.972
you know,

00:03:58.972 --> 00:03:59.439
they're known as

00:03:59.439 --> 00:04:00.540
being more knowledgeable.

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:02.542
The the process encourages

00:04:02.542 --> 00:04:03.943
engagement with voters

00:04:03.943 --> 00:04:04.410
as opposed to

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:05.612
just being kind of a straight up

00:04:05.612 --> 00:04:06.613
straw poll.

00:04:06.613 --> 00:04:08.982
And I wonder, given your experience

00:04:08.982 --> 00:04:10.950
covering so many of these, is Iowa

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:12.919
a place that has a potential

00:04:12.919 --> 00:04:14.187
to stray from Trump? Right.

00:04:14.187 --> 00:04:15.355
To to give another candidate

00:04:15.355 --> 00:04:16.422
an opportunity,

00:04:16.422 --> 00:04:17.357
particularly even one,

00:04:17.357 --> 00:04:18.658
not just a DeSantis candidacy,

00:04:18.658 --> 00:04:19.692
but but someone from

00:04:19.692 --> 00:04:19.959
kind of

00:04:19.959 --> 00:04:21.728
the more mainstream

00:04:21.728 --> 00:04:23.696
or moderate Republican

00:04:23.696 --> 00:04:25.598
strain of the party

00:04:25.598 --> 00:04:26.733
like Nikki Haley or folks

00:04:26.733 --> 00:04:28.034
who are now positioning themselves

00:04:28.034 --> 00:04:28.534
in that lane

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:32.472
Iowa is definitely a place, Jim.

00:04:32.472 --> 00:04:33.606
And you're right

00:04:33.606 --> 00:04:35.975
that new candidates can audition.

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:37.677
You know, they can come.

00:04:37.677 --> 00:04:39.679
They don't have to be the most well-known

00:04:39.679 --> 00:04:41.848
or the party establishment favorite.

00:04:41.848 --> 00:04:43.349
And they can come and get

00:04:43.349 --> 00:04:44.717
because it's a cheap market.

00:04:44.717 --> 00:04:45.618
You don't have to buy

00:04:45.618 --> 00:04:47.120
a lot of advertising.

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:48.721
You can meet people one on one

00:04:48.721 --> 00:04:50.356
and get your message out

00:04:50.356 --> 00:04:51.891
But the Iowa caucuses

00:04:51.891 --> 00:04:53.426
are also not the place

00:04:53.426 --> 00:04:55.862
for moderates necessarily,

00:04:55.862 --> 00:04:58.431
because it requires this engagement.

00:04:58.431 --> 00:05:00.600
You get the activists and the activists

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:02.101
tend to be in the Republican Party

00:05:02.101 --> 00:05:04.137
from the more conservative wing.

00:05:04.137 --> 00:05:05.571
So, you know, it's

00:05:05.571 --> 00:05:07.006
because they have challengers

00:05:07.006 --> 00:05:10.310
running to the right of a lot of times

00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:12.445
what we would see in past cycles

00:05:12.445 --> 00:05:12.945
that, you know,

00:05:12.945 --> 00:05:15.315
the Jeb Bush's or

00:05:15.315 --> 00:05:17.383
other establishment candidates,

00:05:17.383 --> 00:05:19.452
that's where those insurgencies do

00:05:19.452 --> 00:05:20.053
very well.

00:05:20.053 --> 00:05:20.887
Here

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:22.655
we are in the early days,

00:05:22.655 --> 00:05:24.223
obviously, as we know.

00:05:24.223 --> 00:05:25.391
But I'm just I'm curious,

00:05:25.391 --> 00:05:26.793
as you look at this,

00:05:26.793 --> 00:05:29.629
as Iowa once again becomes the center.

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:32.098
Does anything feel different

00:05:32.098 --> 00:05:34.901
this time around or heading into 20, 24

00:05:36.903 --> 00:05:37.303
Yeah.

00:05:37.303 --> 00:05:37.904
Well, first of all,

00:05:37.904 --> 00:05:39.472
the Democrats are not,

00:05:39.472 --> 00:05:40.606
you know, joining them

00:05:40.606 --> 00:05:43.042
joining in on this cycle

00:05:43.042 --> 00:05:45.144
because the Democratic National Committee

00:05:45.144 --> 00:05:47.680
blacklisted in Iowa So normally,

00:05:48.114 --> 00:05:48.448
you know,

00:05:48.448 --> 00:05:49.182
this would be

00:05:49.182 --> 00:05:52.819
a busier cycle with both parties in play.

00:05:53.353 --> 00:05:54.887
Also, I think,

00:05:54.887 --> 00:05:57.090
you know, it's interesting to me

00:05:57.090 --> 00:05:58.858
how unified the candidates

00:05:58.858 --> 00:06:00.393
messages are so far.

00:06:00.393 --> 00:06:02.161
A lot of candidates coming to Iowa

00:06:02.161 --> 00:06:04.330
talking about education

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:06.032
and especially kind of the culture wars

00:06:06.032 --> 00:06:07.133
and education.

00:06:07.133 --> 00:06:08.801
That is what Ron DeSantis talked about.

00:06:08.801 --> 00:06:09.435
That's what

00:06:09.435 --> 00:06:11.371
Nikki Haley spoke about on her

00:06:11.371 --> 00:06:12.572
first trip to Iowa.

00:06:12.572 --> 00:06:13.873
I believe Donald Trump

00:06:13.873 --> 00:06:14.640
will be talking about

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:16.943
education again tonight. As well.

00:06:16.943 --> 00:06:19.946
It's partly I think they might think

00:06:20.146 --> 00:06:21.414
Iowa Republicans want to hear

00:06:21.414 --> 00:06:21.781
that's what

00:06:21.781 --> 00:06:22.749
our legislators spent

00:06:22.749 --> 00:06:25.051
the entire year talking about so far.

00:06:25.718 --> 00:06:27.620
So we'll see what happens.

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:29.856
Kathy, so quickly here, can I ask you,

00:06:29.856 --> 00:06:31.057
is the discussion

00:06:31.057 --> 00:06:32.558
of a possible indictment in New York

00:06:32.558 --> 00:06:33.659
at all,

00:06:33.659 --> 00:06:34.961
a topic of discussion there

00:06:34.961 --> 00:06:36.996
and does that, in your view, help or hurt

00:06:37.397 --> 00:06:38.731
a Trump candidacy in Iowa?

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:41.434
I don't think it

00:06:41.434 --> 00:06:43.636
matters to the electorate

00:06:44.103 --> 00:06:45.538
for the caucuses.

00:06:45.538 --> 00:06:49.142
A lot of those types of things are,

00:06:49.675 --> 00:06:52.779
you know, they attribute it to the media

00:06:52.779 --> 00:06:55.648
or to partizans in the judiciary or the,

00:06:55.815 --> 00:06:57.683
you know, those kinds of things.

00:06:57.683 --> 00:06:58.518
I don't see

00:06:58.518 --> 00:07:00.686
them as taking that terribly seriously.

00:07:00.686 --> 00:07:03.990
But there is a feeling among Republicans

00:07:03.990 --> 00:07:05.758
that Trump has too much baggage.

00:07:05.758 --> 00:07:06.993
And so,

00:07:07.059 --> 00:07:07.260
you know,

00:07:07.260 --> 00:07:08.694
this could be just a little part

00:07:08.694 --> 00:07:09.829
of what they consider

00:07:09.829 --> 00:07:11.964
to be baggage for him.

00:07:11.964 --> 00:07:13.633
Kathie Obradovich, thanks so much.

